  "id": "COMPOUND:19464 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "Dorsmanin D appears to have a complex, multi-target relationship with SF-188, as evidenced by three distinct pathways. The first two paths indicate that Dorsmanin D targets Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 and Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, both of which are involved in the metabolism of 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, a compound that directly targets SF-188. This suggests a potential metabolic pathway where Dorsmanin D modulates the activity of enzymes involved in the biosynthesis or degradation of this compound, ultimately affecting SF-188. The third path reveals an additional target of Dorsmanin D, N-Methyltyramine, which also leads to SF-188. While the exact mechanism of action remains unclear, the shared involvement of 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol in multiple pathways supports a common biological target. The integration of these targets suggests that Dorsmanin D may act through a metabolic or enzymatic pathway that influences SF-188, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism.",
